---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/seo/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description={`Privacy Policy for ${siteConfig.name}: client-side conversion, cookies, AdSense, and GA4 disclosures.`} canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <div class="container content-prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy' }]} />
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta-row">Last updated: <time datetime={siteConfig.lastUpdated}>{siteConfig.lastUpdated}</time></p>
    <div class="answer-box">
      <p>
        File <strong>content</strong> on {siteConfig.name} is processed locally in your browser and is not transmitted to our
        servers for conversion — your file never leaves your device during conversion. That promise is about document bytes,
        not about zero network activity: the page may still load scripts, analytics (when configured), or ad code separately.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2>What we process</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Conversion files:</strong> read only in your browser memory; not uploaded for processing. Verify in DevTools → Network while converting.</li>
      <li><strong>Hosting logs:</strong> standard CDN/host request logs (IP, user agent) may exist on the static host.</li>
      <li><strong>Preference cookies:</strong> e.g. analytics consent (`lf_analytics_consent_v1` = granted or denied).</li>
      <li><strong>Page analytics:</strong> when GA4 is configured, usage metrics load <strong>only after you Accept</strong> the cookie banner; they are not your file contents. Reject keeps GA off.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Google AdSense and advertising cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Ads are <strong>disabled until</strong> a publisher ID is configured in site config. When enabled, Google and
      third-party vendors may use cookies to serve ads based on prior visits to this or other sites. Users can opt out of
      personalized advertising via <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads">Google Ads Settings</a> and
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">aboutads.info</a>. Google uses the DoubleClick cookie for AdSense; see
      Google’s policies for details.
    </p>
    <h2>Google Analytics (GA4)</h2>
    <p>
      GA4 is inactive until `PUBLIC_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID` is set at build time. When enabled, Google’s gtag.js snippet
      loads <strong>only after you click Accept</strong> on the cookie banner. Until then (and if you choose Reject),
      no requests are sent to Google Analytics. Accepted consent is stored in
      <code>lf_analytics_consent_v1</code> so returning visits can load analytics without asking again. You can clear
      site data in your browser to reset the choice. Analytics measure page usage only — never your converted file
      contents. This banner is not a Google-certified CMP for personalized ads in the EEA/UK/CH.
    </p>
    <h2>EEA, UK, and Switzerland</h2>
    <p>
      Personalized ads in these regions require a Google-certified CMP integrated with the IAB TCF. Do not enable
      personalized AdSense for those visitors until a CMP is configured. Setup steps are documented in the repository file
      <code>docs/ADSENSE.md</code>.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
